# ~/.gitignore_global ignores `.claude/` in every repo. This repo is the one
# exception: it *is* the backup for Claude Code's user-level config. Repo-level
# rules take precedence over core.excludesFile, so the negation below works here
# without changing behavior anywhere else.
#
# Re-include the directory so git will descend into it, re-ignore its contents,
# then allowlist only the files that are safe to publish. Anything Claude Code
# drops in .claude/ later (credentials, history, transcripts, caches) stays
# ignored by default -- add new entries here deliberately, one at a time.
!.claude/
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/statusline-command.sh

# Same story: ~/.gitignore_global ignores CLAUDE.md everywhere, and this repo is
# the exception -- the guidance belongs with the code it describes.
!CLAUDE.md
